From d85bead5d209abfaa865fe8ad8390b6a04c3402a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kudbee <twd4lifez@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:15:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(infra): correct upctl tooling; record live UpCloud
 substrate audit (#280)

verify_upcloud_cli.py could never pass: it ran `upctl --version` (exits
100) and required ~/.upcloud/config (a file upctl never reads), and it told
users to `pip install upcloud-cli` (PyPI 404; upctl is a Go binary). The
rewrite follows the official UpCloudLtd/upcloud-cli docs: `upctl version`,
auth via UPCLOUD_TOKEN / keyring / ~/.config/upctl.yaml, with the repo's
THINKBOX_UPCLOUD_API_TOKEN mapped to UPCLOUD_TOKEN and never printed. It is
live-verified against checksum-verified upctl v3.36.0 and the real API
(account kudbeex). 10 hermetic tests are added. SECURITY_CHECKLIST install/
auth steps, the env table and 3 dead (404) doc links are corrected.

Docs record the live substrate audit:
- two UpCloud accounts (worker-01 lives in `kudbee`, hence
  SERVER_FORBIDDEN)
- an orphaned duplicate worker-02 from a retried create POST
- worker-01's SSH blocker is auth-only
- the active worker-02 00e300f7 is LIVE VERIFIED

The bridge decision is Option A (a new `upcloud-ssh` substrate in
governed_job_execution). It is blocked by a pre-existing route shadow:
backend.main's legacy api_v1 /run handler hides the governed POST
/api/v1/run in the real app.

